      "text": "Given:\n1. Triangle $ABC$ is with a right angle at $C$\n2. $\\angle BAC < 45^\\circ$, $AB = 4$\n3. Point $P$ on $\\overline{AB}$ such that $\\angle APC = 2\\angle ACP$ and $CP = 1$\n4. We are to find ratio $\\frac{AP}{BP}$.\n\nBy Angle Bisector Theorem,\nLet $PA=a$ and $PB=b$\n$\\frac{AP}{PB} = \\frac{CP}{BC} = \\frac{1}{AC} = \\frac{1}{AB-AC} = \\frac{1}{4-AC}$.\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{AB-AC} = \\frac{1}{4-AC}\n\\]\n\nBy side formula: \n$\\frac{1}{a}+\\frac{1}{b} = \\frac{1}{b+a}$\n$\\frac{a+b}{a\\times b} = \\frac{1}{b+a} \\implies a\\times b = a+b$\n$\\boxed{\\frac{AP}{BP} = \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{1-\\sqrt{2}}}$\n\n\\[\n\\frac{AP}{BP} = \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{1-\\sqrt{2}}\n\\]\nThus, ratio ratio $\\frac{AP}{BP}$ in the wiev of the given form can be written as $\\boxed{\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{1-\\sqrt{2}}}$\n\nSo, we import find $p+q+r$ for the final answer \n$\\frac{AP}{BP} = \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{1-\\sqrt{2}} = \\boxed{4}$.",
